# Privacy Policy – TrackFlow

**Effective Date:** 8 November 2026  
**Developer:** Adarsh Gupta  
**Contact Email:** contact.flutterdeveloper@gmail.com

## 1. Introduction

Welcome to TrackFlow.

TrackFlow is a productivity application designed to help users manage tasks, categories, notes, reminders, notifications, and daily activities.

Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains what information may be collected, how it is used, how it is stored, and how you can request its deletion.

By using TrackFlow, you agree to the practices described in this policy.

## 2. Information We Collect

Depending on the features you use, TrackFlow may process the following information:

### Account Information
- Name
- Email address
- Profile information
- Authentication information provided through Firebase Authentication or Google Sign-In

### Task and Productivity Information
- Task titles and descriptions
- Categories and priorities
- Task dates and times
- Reminder preferences
- Completion status
- Notes and folders
- Notification preferences

### Files and Attachments
- PDF attachment names and file locations
- Files selected or stored locally on your device

### Technical Information
- Basic app diagnostics and crash information
- Device and app information processed by the services used by the application

## 3. How We Use Your Information

We use information to:

- Create and manage your account.
- Save and synchronize tasks, notes, categories, and notifications.
- Provide reminders and productivity features.
- Maintain app functionality and improve performance.
- Provide AI-powered assistance when you choose to use AI features.
- Respond to support and account deletion requests.

## 4. Third-Party Services

TrackFlow uses or may use the following third-party services:

### Firebase Authentication
Used for email/password authentication and Google Sign-In.

### Cloud Firestore
Used to store and synchronize account-related information, including tasks, notes, categories, and notifications.

### Firebase AI / Google AI
When you use AI-powered features, the text or information you submit for that feature may be processed by Google's AI services to generate a response.

### Firebase Storage
If profile-image upload functionality is enabled and used, the selected image may be stored using Firebase Storage.

These services are operated by their respective providers and are subject to their own privacy policies and terms.

Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

Firebase Privacy Information: https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy

## 5. Local Data Storage

Some information, including notes, categories, attachments, and other app data, may be stored locally on your device.

Local notifications are used to provide task reminders.

Uninstalling the application may not automatically remove every item stored by external services. Use the account deletion option when you want to request deletion of your account and associated app data.

## 6. Data Sharing

TrackFlow does not sell your personal information.

Information may be processed by the third-party service providers described in this policy when required to provide app functionality, authentication, synchronization, or AI features.

We do not intentionally share personal information with unrelated third parties for their own marketing purposes.

## 7. Data Security

We use services and reasonable measures intended to protect your information.

However, no method of electronic storage or transmission is completely secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security.

## 8. Account and Data Deletion

You can request deletion of your TrackFlow account and associated data.

### In-App Deletion
1. Open TrackFlow.
2. Go to your Profile.
3. Select **Delete Account**.
4. Complete the confirmation process.

The deletion process is designed to remove your Firebase Authentication account, associated Firestore data, and supported local app data. Associated profile images will also be included if they are stored through Firebase Storage and the deletion service supports their removal.

### Request Deletion by Email
If you experience any problem deleting your account through the application, you can send a deletion request to:

**contact.flutterdeveloper@gmail.com**

Please send the request from your registered email address and mention that you want your TrackFlow account deleted.

We may need to verify account ownership before processing the request. Never send your password.

Some information may remain temporarily in backups or be retained where required by applicable law or legitimate security requirements.

## 9. Children's Privacy

TrackFlow is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information, please contact us so that we can review the request.

